Dear All,



The mid semester examination of CRE II will be on topics discussed until
the lecture of 11.09.2026. The following materials are part of the syllabus



   - Chapters 7 and 8 of J.M. Smith for Module 1
   - Chapter 10 (until section 10.4.4) of H.S. Fogler for Module 2
   - Chapter 18 (until section 18.3) of O. Levenspiel for Module 3. You may
   also refer to Chapter 15 (until section 15.3.1) of H.S. Fogler for
   additional explanation.
   - Tutorials 1, 2 and 3
   - Class Notes until 11.09.2026



For Module 3, although you may not focus on the *solution of the
differential equation* for the determination of the concentration profile
inside the porous catalyst, *the formulation of the problem*, the concepts
of the effectiveness factor (=CE=B7) and Thiele modulus (=CE=A6) should be =
known.



All the best,

Sangram

